#title[English Document]

px-patch is a new patch for OpenTTD, developed on top of OpenTTD JGRPP, which implements:
+ Train decoupling and coupling
+ Modular airports
+ Player-defined, nameable custom order lists, allowing vehicles to execute an order list within their order
+ Options to ban trains from waiting in depots and to ban trains from being serviced at stations

Before reading this documentation, you should already be familiar with OpenTTD and JGR Patches. If you are not yet familiar with the game, you can read the #link("https://wiki.openttd.org/")[OpenTTD documentation] and the #link("https://github.com/JGRennison/OpenTTD-patches/wiki")[JGRPP documentation].

px-patch is open-sourced under the GPL v2 license at #link("https://github.com/pulsexlb/OpenTTD-patches")[GitHub]; the latest version can be downloaded from #link("https://github.com/pulsexlb/OpenTTD-patches/releases/")[GitHub Release] and kept up to date.

*Please note: this branch uses large language models extensively to write code, and the project may be unstable. Please grab the latest version from GitHub Release in time, as it usually contains the newest bug fixes.*
